<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, meal prices steady, soyoil slips.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, meal prices steady, soyoil slips.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down by 500 rupees per tonne on increased selling from solvent plants and poor demand from vanaspati (vegetable oil) manufacturers, they said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were almost steady in thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $280 per tonne for October delivery and was $275-276 per tonne for November, December and January shipment in new season. Rapeseed extraction was $125 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,200 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,150-4,175 rupese FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
